      "role": "user",
      "content": "Got it. So we're looking for that specific mix of poise and assertion. To be practical for our client—since this is a global role—do you think these markers are universal, or are there certain cultural backgrounds where these specific behaviors might actually come across as less effective or even \"wrong\" for an executive? Like, would someone who is naturally more soft-spoken or uses different non-verbal cues struggle to hit that \"commanding\" mark in a Western-style boardroom?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
